.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.\" Manual page of Deskence. Kept by hand; @VERSION@ is filled in by Meson.
.TH DESKENCE 1 "" "Deskence @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deskence \- settings and recovery of the Deskence enhancements for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deskence
.RB [ \-\-page
.IR PAGE ]
.br
.B deskence status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B deskence enable
.RI [ FEATURE ...]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B deskence disable
.RI [ FEATURE ...]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B deskence preset
.RB { list | apply | import | export | undo }
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B deskence reset
.RI [ PART ...]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B deskence diagnostics
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B deskence
.RB { \-\-help | \-\-version }
.br
.B deskence
.I COMMAND
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deskence adds a dock with folders, desktop icons, application icons in the
top bar, a clipboard history and other features to GNOME. Each feature is a
GNOME Shell extension that can be turned on and off on its own.
.PP
Without a command,
.B deskence
opens the settings window;
.B \-\-page
selects a page: general, dock, desktop-icons, app-grid, top-bar, windows or
clipboard.
.PP
The commands below do the same without the window. They never load GTK and
need no display, so they also work on a text console, for example when the
desktop does not start properly. Every command concerns the user running it;
Deskence refuses to run as root and never needs
.BR sudo .
.PP
Settings are stored with GSettings (dconf). A change is
.I saved
when it is written there and
.I applied
when the running GNOME Shell confirmed it. Commands that change features say
which of the two happened.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B dock
The dock, window previews and folders in the dock.
.TP
.B desktop-icons
Icons of the desktop folder on the desktop.
.TP
.B tray
Application icons in the top bar.
.TP
.B app-grid
Alphabetical order of the applications view. It only runs while that order
is chosen.
.TP
.B clipboard
The clipboard history.
.TP
.B keep-awake
The Keep Awake button in the quick settings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
For each feature: whether it is enabled in the saved settings, what it does
in the running GNOME session (running, not running, error, starts after
logging in again, unknown when GNOME Shell cannot be reached), conflicting
extensions and a copy in the home folder that replaces the installed one.
The saved setting alone does not mean that a feature runs.
.TP
.BR enable " " \fIFEATURE\fR... | \-\-all
Turns features on. Through GNOME Shell when it runs (the change is applied
at once), otherwise in the saved settings for the next login. Enabling an
enabled feature changes nothing.
.TP
.BR disable " " \fIFEATURE\fR... | \-\-all
Turns features off. Their settings are kept.
.B \-\-all
means all Deskence features; other extensions and the list of extensions
they are in are never changed.
.TP
.B preset list
The saved presets, with their names and IDs.
.TP
.BI "preset apply " NAME
Applies a saved preset, given by name or ID. It shows what changes and asks
before applying. The settings before it are saved and can be restored with
.BR "preset undo" .
.TP
.BI "preset import " FILE
Checks a preset file (a
.I .json
preset or a
.I .deskence
archive with images) and saves it among the presets. It is not applied
unless
.B \-\-apply
is given. A saved preset of the same name is not replaced unless
.B \-\-replace
is given;
.B \-\-name
saves it under another name. Nothing in a preset is ever run, and presets
never contain the clipboard history.
.TP
.BI "preset export " FILE
Writes the current settings to a file. An existing file is not replaced
unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.B \-\-pinned
includes the pinned applications,
.B \-\-stacks
the folders in the dock and
.B \-\-images
a custom applications button image (the file is then an archive).
.TP
.B preset undo
Undoes the last applied preset: the settings and features it changed return
to their values from before it. A setting changed after the preset was
applied is listed and left as it is, unless
.B \-\-include\-changed
is given. Settings that make one option, such as a custom color and the
color, are undone together. Applying another preset replaces what can be
undone.
.TP
.BR reset " " \fIPART\fR... | \-\-all
Restores default settings. A part is one of dock, desktop-icons, tray,
app-grid, clipboard, keep-awake or windows (the title bar buttons, a GNOME
setting), the same as "Restore Default Settings" on the pages of the
settings window.
.B \-\-all
restores every Deskence setting, like "Restore Default Deskence Settings":
the folders in the dock are removed from it, the applications view returns
to your own order and the
.B app-grid
feature is turned off; the other features stay as they are. The command
lists what changes and asks before restoring. It never deletes files on the
desktop, custom images, saved presets or the clipboard history, and never
changes how the clipboard history is kept. Other settings in dconf are not
touched.
.TP
.B diagnostics
A report for bug reports, in Markdown for a GitHub issue: versions of
Deskence, GNOME Shell and the libraries, the distribution, the kind of
session, monitors (resolution, refresh rate, scale), the saved and running
state of each feature, conflicts and the names of settings that differ from
their defaults; unknown values are shown as unavailable. The settings
window shows, copies and saves the same report. It contains no clipboard contents, window titles, file names,
setting values or private paths, and it is never sent anywhere.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Prints one JSON document on standard output and nothing else. It has the
fields
.B format
("io.github.deskence.Deskence.cli", or
"io.github.deskence.Deskence.diagnostics" for diagnostics),
.B version
(1) and
.BR command ,
and on failure
.B error
and
.BR exit-status .
With
.B \-\-json
no question is asked.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Only shows what would change. No setting and no file is changed.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Confirms the change without a question. Without a terminal (in a script, or
with
.BR \-\-json ),
a change that needs confirming fails unless
.B \-\-yes
is given.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Shows the help of
.B deskence
or of a command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Shows the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done (or nothing to change).
.TP
.B 1
Failed; nothing or not everything was changed. The message says what.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line, for example an unknown feature.
.TP
.B 3
The change needs confirming: it was declined, or there was no terminal and
no
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B 4
Saved, but the running GNOME session did not confirm the change (GNOME Shell
is not running or did not answer). It applies after logging in again.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the state of all features:
.PP
.RS
deskence status
.RE
.PP
Turn the dock off and on again:
.PP
.RS
deskence disable dock
.br
deskence enable dock
.RE
.PP
Save the current settings including pinned applications to a file, and
bring them back on another computer:
.PP
.RS
deskence preset export ~/deskence.json \-\-pinned \-\-stacks
.br
deskence preset import ~/deskence.json \-\-apply
.RE
.PP
See what restoring the dock defaults would change, then do it in a script:
.PP
.RS
deskence reset dock \-\-dry\-run
.br
deskence reset dock \-\-yes
.RE
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
When the desktop does not work properly after logging in, switch to a text
console (for example Ctrl+Alt+F3), log in as the same user and use the
commands below. Logging in on the console gives the commands the same
session bus as the desktop (through
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bus ),
so changes reach a running GNOME Shell. Do not set
.B DISPLAY
or
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
by hand, and do not use
.BR sudo .
When no session bus is available (for example when the user is not logged
in through systemd), the settings cannot be saved and the commands say so
without changing anything.
.TP
1. Check the state
.B deskence status
shows which features are enabled and which run, fail or wait for a new
login.
.TP
2. Turn off a feature that causes problems
.B deskence disable dock
(or another feature). Its settings are kept.
.TP
3. Turn off all of Deskence
.B deskence disable \-\-all
turns off every Deskence feature and nothing else. Closing the settings
window does not turn anything off.
.TP
4. Restore default settings
.B deskence reset dock \-\-dry\-run
shows what changes;
.B deskence reset dock \-\-yes
or
.B deskence reset \-\-all \-\-yes
restores the defaults.
.TP
5. Go back to a preset
.B deskence preset list
and
.BI "deskence preset apply " NAME
apply a saved preset;
.B deskence preset undo
returns to the settings before the last applied preset.
.TP
6. Collect diagnostics
.B deskence diagnostics > deskence-report.txt
for a bug report. Read it before attaching it.
.TP
7. When logging in again is needed
GNOME Shell finds installed extensions only when the session starts: after
installing or updating Deskence, log out and in again. When a command
reports exit status 4 (GNOME Shell was not running or did not answer), the
change applies at the next login. With Wayland, GNOME Shell cannot be
restarted without logging out; Deskence never restarts it or logs you out.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dconf/user
The settings (dconf), under /io/github/deskence/deskence/ and, for the
enabled features, org.gnome.shell enabled-extensions.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/deskence/presets/
Saved presets, one folder each.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/deskence/before-import.json
The settings before the last applied preset, for
.BR "preset undo" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/deskence/
Copies of custom applications button images; the clipboard history in
.I clipboard/
when it is kept after logging out.
.TP
.I /usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/*@deskence.github.io/
The installed features.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/gnome-shell/extensions/*@deskence.github.io/
A copy here replaces the installed feature;
.B deskence status
reports it.
.TP
.I /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/io.github.deskence.Deskence.gschema.xml
The settings schema with all keys and their defaults.
.PP
The folders under
.IR ~/.config ,
.I ~/.local/share
and
.I ~/.local/state
follow
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
and
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
when they are set.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/grochala/deskence/issues and attach the
output of
.BR "deskence diagnostics" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnome-extensions (1),
.BR gsettings (1),
.BR dconf (1)
